  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-29T11:16:58.896Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In relatively populated lobbies of even as low as 10 people, me and others have a substantial mic delay of about 5 seconds for our voices to be outputted to one another. Often my visemes will move seconds before my voice is even transmitted.\n\nThe delay can vary to less time but more often than not, the same or more delay.\n\nI'm experiencing this with around 100-150 max ping (when on NA, I'm EU) and on a gigabit network.\n\nIt's making some convos and first impressions pretty impossible mistakenly interrupt one another.\n\nPS. We have figured out the source of the issue, that this only occurs when a user is alone in a discord call, so may not be an issue with VRChat but the combo of the two. Will leave this post for people to find if they experience this same issue.",
